answer.resp:
{
  "persona": "Your views on social media are shaped by using it a lot as a background habit, especially checking Snapchat and watching what others are doing, while rarely putting your own posts out there. You may look after bedtime sometimes, but you usually stop before it hurts your sleep, and you do not tend to compare yourself negatively. Even so, the quick updates and streaks can feel shallow, so social media can leave you feeling less genuinely connected to friends despite spending many hours on it. Your household has a few loose expectations about phone use, but they are not heavily enforced.",
